# Line endings are decided here, not per machine.
#
# Without this file every Windows clone rewrites all 61 files to CRLF on
# checkout while the objects hold LF, so `git status` reports the whole
# repository as modified — 8598 insertions and 8598 deletions with no content
# change at all. That noise is not harmless: it hid the question "does this
# working tree hold uncommitted work?" twice, and answering it needed a diff
# with --ignore-all-space to prove the changes were empty.
#
# The service runs on Linux and the SQL is executed by Postgres, so LF is the
# right answer in the objects AND in the working copy. eol=lf makes that true on
# every platform instead of depending on how core.autocrlf happens to be set.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Nothing in here is binary today. Declared anyway, because the day someone adds
# a screenshot to the README is not the day to discover that text=auto mangled it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
